      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** That is twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg for prescription ibuprofen. The single dose of 1,600 mg is also above the usual maximum single dose of about 800 mg. Typical adult dosing is 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, with no more than 3,200 mg/day.\n\nThis patient is 70 years old, so NSAID risks such as GI bleeding, kidney injury, and fluid retention are higher, even with normal baseline function.\n\nPlease confirm how you want to proceed:\n1. **Correct the dose**, for example 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or a lower dose such as 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours. I'd suggest the lower end for a 70-year-old.\n2. **Keep 1600 mg four times daily** if you've confirmed it's intentional, in which case I'll enter it with a note documenting the reason.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order."
      }
